        "“They don’t ring,” he said.",
        "“What do you mean they don’t ring? They’re bells.”",
        "“They never have. Not that I’ve heard.”",
        "She looked at him then, steadily, the way women her age looked at men who had stopped making sense, without unkindness, waiting for the rest of it. When it didn’t come, she said, “Then what do you keep them for?”",
        "He thought about it. He wanted to give her an honest answer, because she had always been fair with him, and because it was a fair question, and because no one had asked it in a long time.",
        "“I don’t know,” he said.",
