        "* * *",
        "The station sat by itself at the last crossroads before the country opened all the way up. It had two pumps under a tin canopy and a square of concrete gone green at the edges, and a single window lit inside with the blue light of a cooler. The sun was low by then. The canopy threw a long shadow across the road, and he walked into it and out again, and pushed open the door, and a bell over the door rang.",
        "It was a cheap brass bell on a spring, and it rang the way such bells ring, thin and bright and a little sour, and he stopped in the doorway and stood very still and listened to it until it had stopped.",
        "“Help you?” the clerk said.",
        "He was young, younger than the yard’s youngest driver, with a thin neck and a cap turned backward, and he was sitting on a stool behind the counter with a phone in both hands. He looked up and saw the coat, and the strap across the chest, and the long shape behind the shoulder. His eyebrows went up and stayed up.",
        "A strip of masking tape on his shirt said DEV in marker. The phone in his hands was playing something loud, a flood somewhere, people on a roof, and then, when his thumb moved, a city burning in some war on the far side of the world, and a man laughing at a dog, and a man shouting into a camera that everyone was lying to you, everyone, and then a fire, and his face did not change for any of it. It had the look of a face that had been watching through a window for a long time and had stopped feeling the heat.",
        "“Water,” he said. He had to clear his throat to say it.",
