        "“I don’t know yet,” he said.",
        "“Okay.” The clerk made change. He counted it out into his palm, coin by coin, carefully, the way somebody had once taught him to, and when he was done he did not take his hand back right away. “You walking?”",
        "“Yes.”",
        "“Out that way?” He tipped his head at the window, at the old road going on west into the light.",
