        "“There’s nothing out that way. I mean nothing. Not for like twenty miles. There’s the old grange hall and then there’s a lot of nothing and then there’s the river.” He said it kindly, the way you would tell somebody their shoe was untied. “You want me to call somebody? I can call somebody.”",
        "“No,” he said. “Thank you.”",
        "“It’s going to get dark.”",
        "“I know.” He looked out the window at the pumps, the old road, the light going gold. “I’ve driven past this station for twenty years,” he said. “Every week. I never once came in.”",
