        "Enoch, Hanokh in Hebrew, whose name I spell Hannock. Genesis 5 lists him seventh from Adam, the father of Methuselah and the great-grandfather of Noah, and says only this of him: “Enoch walked with God: and he was not; for God took him” (Genesis 5:24). The Book of Enoch, an ancient Jewish writing kept whole in the Ethiopian church, found in pieces among the Dead Sea Scrolls, and quoted in the Letter of Jude, carried his name forward as a scribe and a witness to what was coming. He gave this book the third name on its cover.",
        "Zeek, the pen name of Steve Dolby, for The Art of Shen Ku: The First Intergalactic Artform of the Entire Universe (Tarcher, 2001). Shen Ku roughly translates as “Pure Traveler” or “Phantom Passenger.” It gave the Traveler a name for the road.",
        "Edgar Cayce and the readings tradition that carries his name, for the questions about reincarnation, karma, and Atlantis that first set me wondering whether a soul could come back to finish what it started, and for the idea of a record kept for the ones who return.",
        "The prophets and the prophecy traditions I read in those years: the rhymes told under Mother Shipton’s name, most of them written long after her, the long argument over Nostradamus, and the Maya teachers who spoke of light returning to a people who had forgotten. They taught me that prophecy can be a warning, not a forecast.",
